// builtins.memql
//
// Deployment-namespace Go-backed builtins. READ-ONLY computation the
// deployment bundle's pure `logic` needs but the MemQL language cannot
// express inline.
//
// suggestNextVersion exists because the next-release-version decision is
// version arithmetic (parse X.Y.Z, increment a part) and MemQL has no native
// string-split / integer-parse. Per the _reference/_logic blessed pattern
// ("a read-only builtin does the mapping"), nextDeploymentVersion
// (logic.memql) delegates the arithmetic here. Pure + deterministic + no side
// effects, so it is safe to call from a logic body under the call-graph
// contract (ADR §2). Backed by integrations/deployversion (mirrors the
// cut-version semver in component/deploycontrol/semver.go).

/// Compute the next release version by bumping a clean three-part numeric version (X.Y.Z; classic
/// semver or CalVer). bump in {major, minor, patch}, default patch; major/minor zero the lower
/// parts. Pure + read-only. Returns { current, bump, next }.
@executor("integration.deployversion.suggestNextVersion")
builtin suggestNextVersion {
  current  string!
  bump     string
}
